Carafe: under Windows, GDBSymbols only fills each block's address map and no longer registers blocks with GDB.
FEX_GDBSYMBOLS makes FEX record every x86 instruction in a block's RIP map, which the profiler needs. FEX also
registers each block with GDB's JIT interface, and on Windows that interface is a stub that ends the process with
"GDBSymbols support not compiled in": the first block compiled raised it inside CompileBlock, and the game hung in
ntdll's unwinder. The registration is now left out on Windows.
MIT, as the file it changes.

--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
@@ -992,9 +992,11 @@ uintptr_t ContextImpl::CompileBlock(FEXCore::Core::CpuStateFrame* Frame, uint64_
         Symbols.RegisterNamedRegion(Thread->SymbolBuffer.get(), CodePtr, DebugData->HostCodeSize, MappedSection->FileInfo.Filename);
       }
 
+#ifndef _WIN32
       if (Config.GDBSymbols()) {
         GDBJITRegister(MappedSection->FileInfo, MappedSection->FileStartVA, GuestRIP, (uintptr_t)CodePtr, *DebugData);
       }
+#endif
     }
   }
 
